WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.200
"Majima Produce"

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:19.450
"This is a work of fiction. The characters,
organizations, and names herein are fictitious,
and bear no relation to existing entities."

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:21.950
Even though we Japanese live
in this country with all its problems,

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.290
"Ikebukuro Chinatown Declaration"

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.290
Even though we Japanese live
in this country with all its problems,

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.660
perhaps we're blessed?

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.790
I'd never thought about that before.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:36.000
But ever since that case,
it's been known to cross my mind.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.200
This time, it's that kind of story.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.620
As you can see, everyone is
enthusiastic about this declaration!

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.160
Here in Ikebukuro, there are
currently over 200 Chinese shops.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.950
The shopkeepers have come together

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:53.290
to declare their vision
for Tokyo's new Chinatown.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:54.750
You're kidding me!

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.700
They won't join the Shopkeeper Association,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.620
and the way they put out
their trash is half-assed.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.750
I am firmly against this Chinatown!

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.830
You're the one who always says
"Quit complaining and get to work."

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:06.830
I <i>am </i>working!

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.750
She can hear me?

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.000
You must be Makoto Majima-san?

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.410
I have a bit of a favor to ask.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:28.250
"Ikebukuro West Gate Park"

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:53.250
Majima-san, you're the only person
in several years who could tell I'm Chinese.

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:55.950
My name is Lin Gaotai.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:00.200
I'm an advisor for technical intern trainees
who come here from China to work.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.750
Technical intern training?

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.580
I was introduced to Takashi Andou-san.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.370
He said there's someone who knows
this town's underworld the best,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.830
and who will act not for money, but for justice.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.580
That would be you, Majima-san.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.910
I have no clue where this is going.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:17.660
A girl has gone missing.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.790
Guo Shungui, age 19.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:28.330
She's a technical intern trainee who works
in an Ibaraki Prefecture sewing factory.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:31.120
I want you to track her down
within a week's time.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.950
You know, it's weird,
how perfect your Japanese is.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:38.700
Pardon me for that. Please, call me Lin.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:43.040
Okay, Lin. This is all so sudden, I'm mixed up.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.120
Majima-san--

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.540
You can call me Makoto.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.870
All right, Makoto.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:49.700
This really isn't easy for me to say.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.910
In one week,

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:55.330
the Ministry of Health, Labour, and Welfare
will inspect the sewing factory.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.910
If Guo isn't there at that time,
it will cause a big problem.

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.660
What big problem?

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:05.830
She and her trainee peers will be
forcibly deported as a penalty.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:09.580
What's up with that?
<i>She's </i>the one who's gone missing.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:15.160
Even so, honest, hard-working
trainees will still be deported.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.950
There are about 250 of them.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:19.700
Two hundred fifty...!

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:24.120
There are many subtle differences
between China and Japan.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:27.160
Two hundred fifty, over just one person...

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.330
"Guaranteed monthly income
of ¥200,000. Work in Tokyo.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.500
Fellow countrymen welcome. --Donglong"

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:41.500
This Donglong is a Chinese
organization in Ikebukuro.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:42.950
Organization?

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:46.410
Trainees go nowhere but the factory
and their dormitories.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:50.330
This flyer was distributed at a
convenience store near the dorm,

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:54.950
so I don't think anyone else
had any contact with Guo.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:57.040
Want to go have some lunch?

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.290
You can fill me in further.

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:01.910
Gladly, Majima-san.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:03.830
Call me whatever you want.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.290
"Nao
Homemade noodles"

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.540
Japanese ramen truly is delicious.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:13.790
I especially enjoy this soy sauce ramen.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:18.000
I don't know much about it, but don't
technical intern trainees from overseas

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.370
have to do difficult, dirty, and dangerous work?

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.750
By Japanese standards, yes.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:28.410
These days, Chinese urbanites
probably couldn't stand it either.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:34.040
Most of the Chinese tourists who come
to Japan are similar to Japanese citizens.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:37.080
But those from rural areas are different.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.660
While the cost of living is lower there,
a farmer's average annual income

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.790
is still no more than several dozen
thousand Japanese yen.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:46.040
<i>Annual </i>income?!

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:51.160
Yes, and that's why there are many
like Guo who frantically study Japanese,

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:57.620
so they can beat the fierce competition
to be chosen as trainees and come to Japan.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.580
They bet on the dream of Japan, the Golden Land.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:05.120
If they do that difficult, dirty, and dangerous
work here for three hard years,

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.410
they can earn 3,000,000 yen.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:11.160
That's equivalent to a
poor farmer's lifetime earnings.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.540
Lifetime earnings...

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:16.200
She is from Henan Province.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:20.700
That region is said to be a symbol
of China's social inequality.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:23.080
They are the same as water.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.000
No matter how much economic development
the country strives toward,

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.660
no matter what measures
the government tries to take,

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:33.330
they end up slipping through the cracks,
like water between fingers.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.160
That is the poverty of China.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.700
She looks kind of angry.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:45.330
That face of hers is one of sickness.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:48.700
The incurable illness called poverty.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.700
Pay up!

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:55.330
We've told you time and again!
No protection money for you!

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:57.450
You owe <i>us </i>for the door!

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.450
If you don't pay, we'll do this!

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.080
You better not disrespect Donglong!

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.660
Hey, knock it off!

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:05.700
Who're you?!

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.160
Please stay out of this, Makoto-san!

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.410
We can handle these punks alone!

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.370
You guys are with Donglong?

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.500
So what if we are?!

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.040
Haven't you ever heard
the term "cultural standard"?

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.830
Whatever that's supposed to mean!

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:22.790
Ow!

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:31.620
Get lost, before I get serious.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.330
--Just you wait!
--You better watch out!

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:36.700
Don't you leave here!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.040
Lin...

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.580
You know kung fu?

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.950
Only a basic knowledge, Majima-san.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:44.500
Is anyone hurt?

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:47.500
Takashi?

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.410
King!

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:49.950
You came by!

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:51.450
We're all fine!

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:54.700
Makoto, come with me.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.830
Lin, you, too.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.540
I got a call from the boss of the Hidaka Group.

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.950
It was information on Donglong.

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:11.450
The Hidaka Group are the people who've
long called the shots in Ikebukuro?

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.540
Right.

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:17.330
He says the Ikebukuro Chinatown Declaration
is a front for Donglong.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.120
What do you mean?

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:23.790
Some Japanese organization is backing Donglong.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:28.160
All we currently know is, it's somehow
connected to the Kansai region.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:32.910
That organization and Donglong
are looking to expand into Ikebukuro.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:36.200
It was Donglong that devised that declaration.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.080
The Chinese shopkeepers
are just being manipulated.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.910
They hardly amount to any real campaign.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:46.080
Those guys earlier were trying
to extort protection money.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:47.870
Thus does Donglong make money,

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:51.750
and that organization takes
some of Donglong's profits.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:54.080
What the hell are you, anyway?

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:57.750
Merely a trainee advisor.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:01.120
Ikebukuro is a free town, it refuses no one.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.370
But a sudden shift in the
power balance invites chaos.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:07.450
Are you saying there'll be a war?

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:08.540
Who knows?

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:12.200
We should run these Donglong
guys out of town already!

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:16.450
It's the Hidaka Group
that will decide that. Not us.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.950
Has the trainee been found?

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:23.500
Not yet. I only just heard
about her this morning.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.580
When you make your move, be careful.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.410
Get out.

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:29.000
At least say "see ya," or something.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.120
"Majima Produce"

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.750
"Majima Produce"

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.750
Are you going to show up here every day
like some office worker?

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.120
Yes, if you don't mind.
Until Guo has been found.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.160
So, where to from here?

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:44.290
If it was a Donglong-related job offer,
I think that means the sex industry.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:49.080
But there's a ton of that
to search through in this town...

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:50.370
Get in.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:52.790
Donglong...

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:53.830
Huh?!

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:56.830
You'll have to be blindfolded
until we reach our destination.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.410
Good day, Donglong representative Yang Feng-san.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:15.870
I am grateful you can spare us
some of your valuable time.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:18.330
I am Lin Gaotai.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:19.450
You know him?

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.330
This is my first time meeting him.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:24.080
Let us be humble and see what happens.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:27.450
I'm the child of a Japanese
left behind in China after the war.

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:30.910
I understand Japanese spoken at any volume.

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:32.000
A thousand pardons.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.750
Where'd you learn Japanese like that?

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:38.250
You're the Henan Province association's advisor?

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:39.620
Henan Province?

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:40.750
Lin, you're also from--

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:45.700
That's right. I am currently
fortunate enough to be an advisor,

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:49.580
but I, too, was originally
a drop of falling water.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:52.830
And you're Makoto Majima.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.040
Your name comes up here and there.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:56.700
Glad to hear it.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:11:00.790
You and I might be dealing
with each other for a long time.

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:03.370
We're only after one thing.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:05.830
Give back Guo! Otherwise...

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:09.830
Aha. So, the Labour Ministry issued a threat.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:11.660
What's he talking about?

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:16.160
Not long ago, the Foreign
Trainee Law was revised.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:22.290
Now, all the trainees won't get kicked out
of the country if one goes missing.

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:23.500
What?

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:28.040
But as ever, there are lots of
factories with terrible conditions.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:32.620
The Labour Ministry is tired
of how ineffective the new law is,

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:36.500
and they try to score points
by issuing yakuza-like threats

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.080
to overly problematic factories.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:45.200
"If our inspection reveals any issues at all,
we're sending everyone back home."

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.410
Isn't that right, Mr. Advisor?

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:51.200
Is it true the factory has lots of problems?

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:53.660
Please return Guo Shungui.

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:55.950
I desire nothing else.

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:57.830
I'll only say this once!

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:00.870
The honor of Donglong's leader
rests on my shoulders.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:03.370
I can't simply send a countryman
who's relying on us

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:06.450
back to a difficult, dirty,
and dangerous labor camp.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.000
So, Guo really <i>is </i>here!

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:12.620
Let me finish speaking, brat!

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:17.000
If you keep poking around,
I can't guarantee you'll survive! Got it?!

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.950
Oh, that was fast.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:30.200
Hey, is the labor camp thing true?

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.160
It <i>is </i>notorious for working the trainees hard

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:36.200
and paying them less than minimum wage.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:40.290
That's why it's true that the
Labour Ministry watches it closely.

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:44.700
But Guo's training period will end soon.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.410
There's no reason for her
to run off at this point.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:50.000
Can I trust you?

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:55.000
Why did you keep quiet about Henan?
As if it has nothing to do with you...

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.370
Tell me the whole story!

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:00.370
Could you have understood if I had?

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:05.870
What would you fortunate Japanese
know of our hellish poverty?

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:09.450
Inside, both of you.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.950
"Episode 5"

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.660
I see.

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:18.870
Lin-chan, you've had it rough.

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:19.700
"Lin-chan"?

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:23.870
Makoto! Lin-chan here came to Japan
from a poor farming family,

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:27.750
and he's worked hard
to finally become an advisor!

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:30.200
I-I just heard him say that.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:35.250
Then for his sake,
go and find that Guo-chan girl!

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:38.580
A thousand thanks, Mother.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:43.540
Oh, you called me "Mother"!
You do know how to make me happy.

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:46.910
You can feel free to think of me
as your Japanese mother, sure.

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:50.790
Oh, I do have a Japanese mother.

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:54.000
Legally, I'm now a naturalized Japanese citizen.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:54.830
Huh?

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.410
When I was toiling away
at a factory in Kawasaki,

00:13:57.410 --> 00:14:02.160
I got to know an old woman
who lived near my apartment.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:07.160
Eventually, she sympathized with
my situation, and she adopted me.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:08.870
That all happened?

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.620
What a wonderful story!

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.160
Makoto! Why're you just sitting there?!

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.540
Get out there and look for Guo-chan!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:21.910
Lin-chan, stop by anytime.
I'll at least treat you to dinner.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.500
Thank you.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:27.250
Man... What a sucker for a sob story.

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:29.870
"50 minutes: ¥15,000"

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:31.950
"Midnight Soapland"

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:36.950
The inspection is the day after tomorrow.

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:41.750
Yeah, but we've got nothing.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:47.370
I'm sure we'll find Guo.
I was forced to use my last resort.

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.830
I should get a phone call soon.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:53.660
<i>Wei.</i>

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.910
Ah, Yang-san.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.950
Yes. Right.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:00.500
Thank you.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.120
<i>Mei guanxi.</i>

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:03.830
"<i>Mei guanxi"</i>?

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:06.790
It means "all right," or "no problem."

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:11.750
Good. The place Guo is at
is the China Doll hostess club.

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:14.580
Yang agreed to release her.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.040
Say what?!

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.540
What kind of trick did you use?!

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:23.750
I asked Yang's superior in Shanghai
to put pressure on him.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:27.910
But I wanted to avoid that approach,
as now I owe China a favor.

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:30.830
Wow, you Chinese guys...

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:34.660
Majima-san, let's go persuade Guo immediately.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:37.040
What if she says she won't go back?

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:40.950
That's when I'd like for <i>you </i>to persuade her.

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.080
Huh?

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:46.540
It's an important job that only you,
a third party, can perform.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:49.330
And that's why you asked for my help?

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:50.500
Quickly, please.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:51.620
Dammit!

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:02.950
I'm Guo Shungui.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:07.870
I'm not connected at all with the Japanese
police or government, so you can relax.

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:11.200
I was sure Lin-san would find me.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.330
But I can't go back!

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:17.660
I need a lot of money, no matter what!

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.580
Could you tell me about it?

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:23.910
I recently got a letter from
my little brother in Henan Province.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:27.540
It said my father's kidney
disease is getting worse.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.450
The only way to save him is a transplant.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:36.790
I had to find some way to quickly
come up with a lot of money!

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:40.290
If I don't, my father will die!

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:44.660
What's that?

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:49.580
It's the first pen I used when
I began studying Japanese.

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:54.000
I used it until the ink ran out,
but I couldn't throw it away.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.830
It's like me, right now.

00:16:56.830 --> 00:17:00.660
I tried so hard, but I had
nothing left in the end.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:04.450
I can't tell you to just let your father die.

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:09.580
But at the same time, continuing to work
illegally doesn't seem like a good idea.

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:12.790
If you don't return to the factory...

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:15.660
...250 trainees will be forcibly deported.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:16.870
No!

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:18.500
I didn't know!

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:21.120
You've got one day left to decide.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:25.870
You can't take your time, but could you
consider it and reach your own decision?

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:30.580
"Majima Produce"

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.040
Good morning, Mother.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:34.910
Oh.

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:38.790
Thank you for putting Guo up for the night.

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:40.700
I picked up a few sweets for you.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.660
Thanks. You're up early.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:47.120
Makoto and Guo-chan went out already.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:50.540
She's decided to go back to Ibaraki.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:53.200
She stayed the night here and thought it over,

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:56.330
and decided she couldn't cause
trouble for all the others after all.

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:57.790
I see.

00:17:57.790 --> 00:18:01.000
She said she wanted to see
Tokyo before she left.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:04.410
Makoto went to show her around.

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:07.660
All she's done is work as hard
as she can this whole time.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:11.160
What a cruel world this is.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:16.500
We're having a farewell party here tonight,
so come by to eat with us.

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:17.950
A thousand thanks.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:29.830
Hi.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.160
Oh, hey, Makoto-san. Are you on a date?

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:34.080
I'm a tour guide.

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:38.660
Wow, from China.

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:39.500
Yes.

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.200
Living overseas isn't easy.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:44.250
I was in Chicago, so I know.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:45.540
Chicago?

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:48.200
Kyouichi was in a Chicago ballet troupe.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.790
He played lead parts, such as the prince.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:54.620
Amazing. It must have
been tough to go that far.

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:59.120
But I doubt it compares to the troubles
she and hers have faced.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:11.040
There are so many buildings
and shiny new cars on the roads.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:14.790
If you get sick, you can go to the hospital
without worrying about money.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:20.120
All the girls are cute, and the
boys seem nice and stylish.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:23.250
Makoto-san, you were born in a fantastic place.

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:25.200
Yeah, maybe I was.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.950
Tomorrow, I'll go back to Ibaraki with Lin-san.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:30.290
Yeah.

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:33.410
My dad's situation is really difficult...

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:36.790
But I'm pretty sure he'll agree with me.

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:41.120
In our family, I also have
a younger brother and sister.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:44.540
We need money for their education, too.

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:49.830
If it's for their future,
I'm sure my dad will see it my way.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:56.580
"Majima Produce"

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:02.870
It's good!

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:05.290
Oh, yeah? Well, eat up.

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:08.580
But, Lin-chan, you're quite the schemer.

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:10.620
Makoto's still just a kid.

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:11.790
A thousand pardons.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:17.580
But now that I've seen how brave Guo-chan is,
how can I say no to your scheme?

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:22.450
I swear I didn't start out planning
to make such an unreasonable request.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:25.330
Huh? What're you two talking about?

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:29.080
Guo-chan's problem is
essentially her legal status.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:33.450
If she became a Japanese citizen,
like Lin-chan, there'd be no more problem.

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:38.160
She wouldn't be deported,
and she'd be free to work in this country.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:41.580
Mom, are you going to adopt Guo?!

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:47.120
Yes. That is, if she agrees.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:51.120
Besides, I've been looking
at her hands since yesterday.

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:59.160
Given the chance, I bet those hands
would do some fine work.

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:02.870
And I can't just stand by
and let your father die.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:04.500
How about it, Guo-chan?

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:08.790
Even if it's just on paper,
would you like to be Makoto's sister?

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:14.450
We're not all that wealthy, but you
could have a dinner like this anytime.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:22.450
Thank you!

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:27.750
If I can do that, I'll work as hard
as I can and support my father!

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:32.000
Can I really stay here in this town?!

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:33.410
Yep.

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:34.410
Lin...

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:37.700
You brought up adoption the
other day on purpose, didn't you?

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:41.040
I truly am grateful for all you've done.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:42.370
<i>Xiexie.</i>

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:46.040
Wow, dude...

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:51.750
The following day, Lin started
the process for Guo's adoption.

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:56.750
It will take some time, of course, but for now,
her trainee contract is cancelled,

00:21:56.750 --> 00:22:00.370
and nothing bad happened to her
or the rest of the 250.

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:03.660
Growing up rolling around
in the alleys of this town,

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:07.580
it never even crossed my mind
that I was blessed.

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:13.080
But when I suddenly gained a sister thanks
to my sentimental mother, I thought:

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:17.200
Even though we Japanese live
in this country with all its problems,

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:19.120
perhaps we <i>are </i>blessed?

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:19.950
<i>What's up</i>

00:22:19.950 --> 00:22:23.080
<i>A world where guys with plans</i>
<i>are the first to fade away</i>

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:25.790
<i>The thought hit me after being out all night</i>

00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:28.620
<i>A gulf forms with the respectable types</i>

00:22:28.620 --> 00:22:31.750
<i>The MIC you nervously gripped</i>

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:34.370
<i>Leave it behind on the stage</i>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:37.450
<i>Unable to trust in the next move</i>

00:22:37.450 --> 00:22:40.410
<i>You get down off the stage of dreams</i>

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:43.200
<i>Fade away from the bustle of the scene</i>

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:46.120
<i>Do you know what becomes of him after that?</i>

00:22:46.120 --> 00:22:49.250
<i>In fact, are you even prepared to know?</i>

00:22:49.250 --> 00:22:52.000
<i>Now that we're involved,</i>
<i>I want to watch you take off</i>

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:54.750
<i>From the runway you chose</i>

00:22:54.750 --> 00:22:58.750
<i>If we happen to meet again today or tomorrow</i>

00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:02.410
<i>Somewhere on this Earth</i>

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:03.870
<i>Let's have fun freestyling</i>

00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:06.950
<i>Like we did that time</i>

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:09.620
<i>What's up</i>

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:11.120
<i>After the live show</i>

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:12.620
<i>In a train window</i>

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:14.000
<i>A brother's face, I find</i>

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:15.500
<i>Comes suddenly to mind</i>

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:18.500
<i>Right now, I don't feel like</i>
<i>lookin' back on the past</i>

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:21.370
<i>But no way in hell am I forgettin' it</i>

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:22.830
<i>After the live show</i>

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:24.330
<i>In a train window</i>

00:23:24.330 --> 00:23:25.750
<i>A brother's face, I find</i>

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.200
<i>Comes suddenly to mind</i>

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:30.120
<i>Right now, I don't feel like</i>
<i>lookin' back on the past</i>

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:33.450
<i>But no way in hell am I forgettin' it</i>
